==Battleground==
*5 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Alpacky]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Doremi]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn, delay 6.67~20 seconds<sup>200f~600f</sup>.
**1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns.

==Strategy==
The essence of this stage is to wipe out the initial enemies to boost income, then hit the enemy base. Do your best to stunlock and annihilate Doremi with fast-attacking and strong units before she destroys your base, then simply finish off Kurosawah and win the stage. [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] trivializes this stage, simply lure Doremi to your base and let Bahamut end her with ease.

Alpacky's strengthen and survive abilities can actually work in favor of any strategy. When Alpacky activates both abilities, she will easily take out anything she hits. After ensuring all five Mr. Angels are defeated, simply fire any kind of [[Cat Cannon]] that deals damage to eliminate Alpacky, and you're free to save up and upgrade the [[Worker Cat]] until you deploy a Cat to hit the base.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - Awakened Bahamut is a fast rusher that delivers rapid and devastating attacks at short range. As mentioned earlier, he trivializes the stage since he alone can effectively stunlock Doremi and stop her from attacking at all. Once Doremi has been slain, you've pretty much won, and Bahamut can help you finish the rest quickly.
**Bahamut's [[Explosion]] [[Talents|Talent]] will interfere this stucklock effect, as Doremi will likely stagger again when she gets displaced into Bahamut's third blast on the edge. This often leads to Bahamut advancing unnecessarily before being nuked by Kurosawah before Doremi is slain. This can be rectified with Attack Up [[Cat Combo]]s.
***Level 50 Awakened Bahamut Cats must use an Attack Up M Cat Combo like [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan]].
***Level 40 Awakened Bahamut Cats are recommended to use one Attack Up (M) combo, and one Attack up (Sm) Cat Combo if available. Otherwise, two Attack Up (Sm) Cat Combos will suffice, although less effective.
*[[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Island Cat]] - Although there are no [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red Enemies]] in this stage, a sufficiently upgraded Manic Island can still be helpful as a cost-efficient melee attacker to wipe out the initial enemies without draining too much resources.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Greater Balrog does extreme damage, on par with Bahamut and can easily stun-lock Doremi. Just beware of his single target attack.
*[[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolic Gao]] and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]]: These units can absolutely demolish Doremi with their anti-[[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] abilities if you lure her close and then keep her at bay. Nevertheless, they are only to act as support since they alone cannot hold back Doremi.
*A combination of units with high DPS and attack rate, especially with Anti-Traitless abilities.

