==Trivia==
*First Errand is a reference to ''Hajimete no Otsukai'' (はじめてのおつかい, "My First Errand"), the Japanese name of ''[[wikipedia:Old Enough!|Old Enough!]]''. The show is about children going out into the world to run their very first errands (with a camera crew following close behind).
**First Errand's Japanese name (はじめてのお使い) is exactly the same as ''Old Enough!''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s, except with ''Otsukai'' (Errand) written in kanji (お使い) instead of hiragana (おつかい).
**[[Doremi]]'s name could be derived from "[https://youtu.be/dpVhzTivUZo Do Re Mi Fa Daijōbu]", the show's opening theme by [[wikipedia:B.B. Queens|B.B.Queens]].

*The stage's name could be a reference to the composer "Babyface"

